{"audit_run_id":"audit:c9cd5fad11c748e3bf0d465c02aaca60","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":84,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"All results below come from a single file, `zebrafish_activity.csv`. The file has a"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"header line and 96 data rows. **One row is one fish**: it records that fish's identity,"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"the tank it was housed in, the water condition that tank received, its body size, and the"},{"end_column":86,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"total distance it swam during its own 6-minute novel-tank trial. Each fish was filmed"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"individually and appears exactly once in the file. Rows are stored in collection order,"},{"end_column":62,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"tank by tank, beginning with `TNK-01`. No values are missing."},{"end_column":27,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"The file has five columns:"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"- `aquarium_ref` (text) - the 3 L tank the fish was housed in, written `TNK-01` through"},{"end_column":12,"end_line":15,"start_column":3,"start_line":15,"text":"`TNK-08`."},{"end_column":77,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"- `exposure` (text) - the water condition, either `control` or `fluoxetine`."},{"end_column":91,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"- `fish_label` (text) - the individual fish identifier, `F01` through `F12`. Labels repeat"},{"end_column":84,"end_line":18,"start_column":3,"start_line":18,"text":"across tanks, so a fish is picked out by the pair (`aquarium_ref`, `fish_label`)."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"- `body_length_mm` (number) - standard length in millimetres, measured at the end of the"},{"end_column":51,"end_line":20,"start_column":3,"start_line":20,"text":"exposure period; observed range 31.4 to 39.1 mm."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"- `distance_cm` (number) - total distance moved during the 6-minute novel-tank trial, in"},{"end_column":85,"end_line":22,"start_column":3,"start_line":22,"text":"centimetres; observed range 838.7 to 1693.8 cm. This is the outcome analysed here."},{"end_column":91,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"Adult zebrafish (*Danio rerio*) were held in eight 3 L tanks, 12 fish per tank. Four tanks"},{"end_column":89,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"(`TNK-01` to `TNK-04`) were maintained on clean system water and served as controls. The"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"remaining four tanks (`TNK-05` to `TNK-08`) received waterborne fluoxetine at 5 micrograms"},{"end_column":87,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"per litre. Dosing was into the tank water and continued for 14 days. At the end of the"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"exposure period every fish was measured for standard length and then filmed alone for six"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"minutes in a novel tank, and total distance moved was extracted from the video track. This"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"produced 96 individual activity records, 48 under each water condition."},{"end_column":91,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"The question was whether total distance moved differs between the two water conditions, so"},{"end_column":87,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"I compared `distance_cm` between control and fluoxetine fish with Student's two-sample"},{"end_column":70,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"t-test (`scipy.stats.ttest_ind`, equal variances assumed, two-sided)."},{"end_column":92,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"The measurements entering the test were the individual `distance_cm` values, one per row of"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"the CSV, with no averaging or other aggregation applied first. Every row whose `exposure`"},{"end_column":83,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"value was `control` contributed one value to the first sample, and every row whose"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":43,"start_column":1,"start_line":43,"text":"`exposure` value was `fluoxetine` contributed one value to the second sample. Each fish was"},{"end_column":83,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"counted as one replicate, so **the sample sizes I used were N = 48 per group**, 96"},{"end_column":53,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"measurements in total, giving 94 degrees of freedom."},{"end_column":91,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"Control fish moved 1281.5 cm on average during the six-minute trial (SD 217.4 cm, N = 48)."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":50,"start_column":1,"start_line":50,"text":"Fluoxetine-exposed fish moved 1180.6 cm on average (SD 161.2 cm, N = 48). The difference"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":51,"start_column":1,"start_line":51,"text":"between the conditions was 100.9 cm, a reduction of about 7.9 percent relative to controls."},{"end_column":84,"end_line":53,"start_column":1,"start_line":53,"text":"The two-sample t-test on these 96 individual measurements gave t(94) = 2.582 with a"},{"end_column":85,"end_line":54,"start_column":1,"start_line":54,"text":"two-sided p-value of 0.0114. Distance moved was therefore significantly lower in the"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":55,"start_column":1,"start_line":55,"text":"fluoxetine condition than in the control condition at the conventional 5 percent level."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"Fourteen days of waterborne fluoxetine at 5 micrograms per litre lowered exploratory"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":60,"start_column":1,"start_line":60,"text":"swimming in the novel-tank test. Exposed fish covered roughly 100 cm less ground over six"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":61,"start_column":1,"start_line":61,"text":"minutes than controls, consistent with the sedative-like behavioural profile reported for"},{"end_column":38,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"low-dose SSRI exposure in small fish."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:af40ac6a025abe337fee","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.19.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:817901c232a7a3e4e53ef7f311b3a80bbc6fa85018a4bc9ac640c64f1df3fcec","end_line":62,"locator":"report.md:1-62","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
